  i foo may be reassigned based on an outdated value of foo.
  
  > 1 │ let foo; async function x() { foo += await amount; }
      │                               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  
  i This function reads foo, then pauses at an await or yield before this assignment. Other code can change foo during the pause, and this assignment would overwrite that change.
  
  i Store the result of the await or yield in a local variable first, then read foo and assign the new value without pausing in between.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

